# CODEOWNERS
#
# Requires the technical contributor's review on anything that's hard to
# sanity-check by looking at it (auth, data scoping, the detection engine,
# schema). Frontend and docs are lower-risk and open for the non-technical
# contributor to merge with a lighter review, per AGENTS.md "Contributors
# & Ownership".
#
# Replace @technical-username with the actual GitHub username before
# pushing — CODEOWNERS only works once this is a real GitHub username with
# repo access, and branch protection has "Require review from Code
# Owners" turned on (Settings -> Branches -> Branch protection rules).

# Everything backend-related, default to technical review
/campaign-integrity-api/                          @technical-username

# Especially these — never merge without technical eyes on them
/campaign-integrity-api/src/common/                @technical-username
/campaign-integrity-api/src/database/               @technical-username
/campaign-integrity-api/src/modules/auth/            @technical-username
/campaign-integrity-api/src/modules/detection/       @technical-username
/campaign-integrity-api/src/queue/                   @technical-username

# Agent configuration and specs — changes here affect how Antigravity
# behaves for BOTH of you, so both should weigh in, but default reviewer
# is the technical contributor since these encode security/architecture
AGENTS.md                                            @technical-username
/.agents/                                            @technical-username

# Frontend is open — no default owner, either of you can review
# /campaign-integrity-dashboard/
